## Ideas
Pick the items that round-trip byte for byte in `.opf.md`:
- `<!-- include: ./intro.opf.md#2,5-7 -->` includes slides from another file (Slidev `src:`), resolved locally within the asset boundary;
- `::left::` / `::right::` sugar for `region=` blocks;
- a short split-image syntax for an image placed at a slide edge (Marp `![bg left]`), so it doesn't need a YAML fence;
- a generated agenda slide built from `section` values (Slidev `<Toc>`);
- code line numbers and code-from-file (`<<< ./file.js#region`).

## Why
These make hand-written decks and the Marp/Slidev imports (opf#506) lossless more often, so less content falls back to `opf-slide`/`opf-block` fences.

## Constraint
The dialect stays small and canonical.

